#
# cppcheck suppressions.  Each one names a finding that is correct about the
# code and wrong about the intent; anything not listed here is a real report.
# Prefer an inline `// cppcheck-suppress <id>` with a reason when the exception
# is local to one line - this file is for the ones that are project-wide.

# cppcheck does not follow system headers by default, and we do not want it to:
# the ETL and yaml-cpp headers are not ours to fix.
missingIncludeSystem
missingInclude

# Public API.  A library exists to be called from outside this repository, so
# "nobody in this tree calls it" is not a defect.
unusedFunction

# fms/limits.hpp exposes its capacities as overridable macros on purpose, and
# the config parser has plenty of branches a given build never takes.
unmatchedSuppression

# Anything the dependency tree drags in.
*:*/_deps/*
*:*/build/*
*:*/build-*/*
